# Project plan is the persistence layer

`GeigerNode Firmware Development.md` is the main development plan for this repository. Every agent working here follows it.

At the start of a task, read that file and continue from PROJECT STATUS. Do not jump ahead of the current phase or checkpoint.

You may edit that file so the next agent can see where the project is. Update PROJECT STATUS when any of these change:

- current phase or the next allowed task
- a checkpoint result (pass, fail, or measurement)
- a decision later sessions must keep
- a blocker, or the exact point where work stopped

Leave the numbered hardware, safety, fuse, and architecture sections unchanged unless the user changes those requirements. A status note does not override HV, fuse, or bring-up safety rules.

Do not create a second plan file. If PROJECT STATUS and a numbered section disagree, the numbered safety rules win and PROJECT STATUS must be corrected.

```text
Where we are:
- Phase 2 firmware flashed. LED on PD7 blinks. PB1 measured LOW.
- Stopped before Phase 3. Fuse write still needs human approval.
```
